From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] treewide: build only for Linux 6.18 and 7.3

Drop every LINUX_VERSION_CODE branch for kernels older than 6.18 and
fold the per-version compatibility patches into this one. compat.h goes
too: its users say const and strscpy() directly and include
<linux/vmalloc.h> where they call it.

The IGS mirred action counts overlimits with
tcf_action_inc_overlimit_qstats(), which 7.3 kept when it renamed
qstats_overlimit_inc().

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---

